tanks  helicopters  personnel carriers  tens of millions of dollars worth of  equipment all destroyed  and these are just a small portion of  the losses suffered by one of the most  powerful armies in the world  when russia began its offensive it hoped  to capture ukraine's capital kiev within  days  but ukraine's army withstood the assault  evidently the russian army has  endemic problems with morale  with its equipment  with its training and its doctrine  and as a result rasul to answer your  question directly russia has been  defeated in the field to a point where  it was effectively routed from the north  of the country  ukrainian armed forces have taken  advantage often ambushing russian troops  and columns  in less than two months since russia  invaded ukraine its military has lost  thousands of soldiers according to  ukrainian officials it's more than the  united states did in its 20 years of war  in afghanistan and nearly a decade in  iraq combined they say russia has lost  at least  479 tanks  496  infantry fighting vehicles  20 aircrafts  4 ships 32 helicopters  trucks vehicles and jeeps in total the  russians have lost nearly 3 000 pieces  of equipment  and these are considered conservative  estimates  the highest profile lost to date was the  moscow the flagship of russia's black  sea fleet losing a flagship is in during  a war is well really bad it's a bad pr  it's bad it's going to  expand  increase the morale of the ukrainians at  the time when they are on the verge of  losing  marijuana  while many things can be said to have  gone wrong for russians general valerie  says the ukrainian armed forces had a  secret weapon  the mobilization of our society and  people's resistance our pilots who are  older than 60 years old come out and ask  for jets they retired from the armed  forces a long time ago and asked give us  planes and we will destroy the russians  so morale is our formula for success  ukrainian forces have employed new  tactical weapons given 